       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg for extended-release). The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg PO once or twice daily.** This would be 1,700 mg/day or 3,400 mg/day. 3,400 mg/day is still over the maximum, so only the once-daily schedule is within the label.\n\nThe intended dose may also have been a typo, for example 850 mg instead of 1,700 mg. Tell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
