       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose. 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, and the FDA-approved label maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. I can't verify that the label says otherwise, and the numbers don't support it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg PO once daily with a meal.** This is 1,700 mg/day.\n\nIf you think a dose above the label maximum is clinically necessary, that decision needs to go through pharmacy and your prescriber or attending review process. It shouldn't be entered through me. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
